  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Family Reunification and Re-integration of Street Children in Kinshasa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poverty and accusations of witchcraft have driven 25,000 boys and girls onto Kinshasa&#x2019;s streets. They miss out on school and face violence from police and older youth. Many end up in gangs, drugs and sex work.    Day and night, staff meet children on the streets. A day centre for boys and a shelter for girls provide meals, counselling, catch-up education and health care. The project works with police, market traders, church leaders and older youth &#x2013; helping the youth earn their own income. It reunites children with families; and gives their mothers a small business loan.    As a result, people treat the children better. Older youth stop abusing them. Children stay at home and in school.</narrative>
  </description>
